{"ref":"BDB, זֹה","hw":"זֹה","html":"† <big><big><span dir=\"rtl\">זֹה</span></big></big>  <em>this</em> (f.) = <span dir=\"rtl\">זֹאת</span> <strong>(</strong>cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, זוֹ²\" href=\"/BDB,_זוֹ²\", dir=\"rtl\">זוֹ</a>, in Mish. the regular fem. of <span dir=\"rtl\">זֶה</span><strong>)</strong>—<a data-ref=\"II Kings 6:19\" href=\"/II_Kings.6.19\">2 K 6:19</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 40:45\" href=\"/Ezekiel.40.45\">Ez 40:45</a> <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 2:2\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.2.2\">Ec 2:2</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 2:24\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.2.24\">24</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 5:15\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.5.15\">5:15</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 5:18\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.5.18\">18</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 7:23\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.7.23\">7:23</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ecclesiastes 9:13\" href=\"/Ecclesiastes.9.13\">9:13</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">זאת</span> does not occur in Ec); also in the phr. <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּזֹה וְכָזֶה</span> (v. <a data-ref=\"BDB, זֶה\" href=\"/BDB,_זֶה\", dir=\"rtl\">זה</a> <strong>6 c</strong> β).","next":"BDB, זוֹ","prev":"BDB, זֶה"}